# The cluster's options for ./gr8 glm53 on bare metal (docs/DEPLOY.md): copy to cluster.env (in the repo root or
# config/) on every box, or pass @<file>. ./gr8 glm53 parses it (KEY=value lines; no $ expansion). The command line wins
# over it, and it wins over the environment. Every box must end up with the same cluster options; per-box values
# (paths, PROXY_CPU) may differ. Two settings are required, the model and how the boxes find each other; every other
# line is optional and has a default (KNOBS.md lists them all). The comments say where TP=3, 4 and 6 differ.

# --- the boxes --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The boxes' LAN addresses, in rank order: three to six of them. The first is the head: the front end and the shim
# run there. Every box lists the same addresses in the same order, and the TP is the number of addresses.
PEERS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3,10.0.0.4
# Or let mentat find the boxes (the default when PEERS is unset): MENTAT=localhost, and TP set to 3, 4, 5 or 6.
#MENTAT=localhost
#TP=4
# TP=3 or 4 without a switch: the boxes cabled in a ring, each box's f0 port to the next box's f1 (in PEERS order).
#SHAPE=ring

# --- the model --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The exlr8 release on Hugging Face. Each box fetches only its own part into MODEL_CACHE, its local disk, and boots
# from there (./gr8 glm53 prepare fetches ahead of time). A local copy of the release also works.
MODEL=https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/glm-5.3-exlr8-k2-k3-k4
MODEL_CACHE=/opt/gr8/cache
# Or let the box's model-loader fetch it (github.com/kindlingai/model-loader; docs/DEPLOY.md, "With model-loader"):
# its socket, and MODEL_CACHE its store, which gr8 only reads. Setting MODEL_LOADER selects it.
#MODEL_LOADER=unix:/var/lib/model-loader/model-loader.sock
#MODEL_CACHE=/var/lib/model-loader
# TP=4: the DFlash2 drafter, fetched and converted on each box. Without it, TP=4 drafts with MTP only. TP=3, 5 and 6:
# remove this line. The drafter's 8 KV heads do not split three, five or six ways, so they draft with MTP (TP=6 runs
# the drafter's whole body on every box with DFLASH=1).
DRAFTER=https://huggingface.co/incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2
# The expert widths: home (3.25 bpw) by default at TP=4, 5 and 6, bit225 (2.25 bpw) at TP=3, where home does not fit
# next to a KV pool. ./gr8 models lists the others.
#VARIANT=home

# --- this box ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working directory: bin/, out/, s2/, run/. Defaults to the repo checkout. Boxes without the CUDA toolkit: build with
# BUNDLE_LIBS=1 (scripts/build.sh); the engine finds cuBLAS in bin/lib.
#G6_HOME=/opt/gr8
# CPU core for this rank's fabric proxy thread (GB10 has 20 cores, 0-19).
#PROXY_CPU=19

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP port of the OpenAI-compatible front end on the head.
#PORT=8100
# Each box finds its two RoCE v2 addresses itself (rail 0 is the lower). Set these to pin them, without SHAPE=ring: the
# address of every rank on fabric rail 1 and rail 2.
#IPS=10.0.1.1,10.0.1.2,10.0.1.3,10.0.1.4
#IPS2=10.0.2.1,10.0.2.2,10.0.2.3,10.0.2.4
# Any launch knob (KNOBS.md), for example a smaller KV pool when a box runs short of memory:
#CAP=262144

# TP=5 tuned for a 617K context (T5X): recipes/tp5-t5x/T5X.env, and docs/TP5-SERVE.md.
